<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring bids mostly higher.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring bids mostly higher.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat cash bids were higher late Monday largely reflecting gains in Minneapolis Grain Exchange spring wheat futures, dealers said.</p>
<p>Movement was mixed. Montana dealers reported farmer selling on &quot;No Price Established&quot; contracts, by which the farmers sell the grain to elevators and set the sale price later.</p>
<p>Spring wheat harvesting was largely completed from the northern Plains to the Pacific Northwest as was planting of winter white wheat in Washington.</p>
<p>MGE December spring wheat gained five cents to end at $4.12-3/4 per bushel.</p>
